# Manual setup steps: things no script can do (privacy permissions, sign-ins, MDM
# apps, settings that aren't exposed via `defaults`). This file is the single source
# of truth for them. It is read by:
#   scripts/manual-steps.sh list | open | check   (numbered checklist, walk-through, checks)
#   install.sh / bootstrap.sh                      (print the checklist at the end)
#   check.sh                                       ("Manual steps" section)
# README.md shows a copy generated by `scripts/manual-steps.sh list --markdown`.
#
# Format (pipe-delimited, one step per line):
#   id | group | title | where | open | check
#   id:    unique kebab-case id
#   group: heading the step is listed under (keep a group's steps together)
#   title: what to do, in plain English
#   where: where to do it (System Settings paths use macOS 27 names)
#   open:  what `manual-steps.sh open` opens, or empty:
#            x-apple.systempreferences:<pane>  a System Settings pane
#            https://… | macappstore://…   a web page / the App Store
#            app:<App Name>                 open -a "<App Name>"
#   check: how `manual-steps.sh check` verifies it (always read-only), or empty = check by hand:
#            tcc:<Service>:<bundle-id>      allowed in the system TCC database (kTCCService<Service>);
#                                           reading it needs Full Disk Access, else check by hand
#            defaults:<domain>:<k=v>[,k=v]  every key reads back as that value
#            app:<path>                     path exists (@HOME@ -> $HOME)
#            logi:<id>[,<id>]               Logi Options+ values match lib/logi-expected.list
#                                           (read from a temp copy of settings.db by
#                                           lib/logi-settings.py; never written)
#            @check.sh                      verified by its own check.sh section (not repeated here)
#            hammerspoon-ax | karabiner-driver | pointer-size | input-british | op-cli | gh-auth
#                                           named checks implemented in scripts/manual-steps.sh
# Blank lines and lines beginning with # are ignored. Fields must not contain '|'.

# ---- Sign-ins ----
gh-auth|Sign-ins|Sign in to the GitHub CLI (needed to clone this private repo)|Terminal: gh auth login||gh-auth
apple-account|Sign-ins|Sign in with your Apple Account (your @icloud.com Apple ID)|System Settings → Apple Account|x-apple.systempreferences:com.apple.systempreferences.AppleIDSettings|
icloud-sync|Sign-ins|iCloud: Photos, iCloud Drive, Messages and other unused sync Off; Passwords (iCloud Keychain) and Find My On|System Settings → Apple Account → iCloud|x-apple.systempreferences:com.apple.systempreferences.AppleIDSettings|
app-store|Sign-ins|Sign in to the App Store (brew bundle needs it for WhatsApp and the other mas apps)|App Store → Store → Sign In|macappstore://|

# ---- Company apps (MDM) ----
mdm-apps|Company apps (MDM)|Install Okta Verify and 1Password from Iru Self Service (Kandji), not Homebrew|Applications → Iru Self Service|app:Iru Self Service|@check.sh
1password-signin|Company apps (MDM)|Sign in to 1Password and unlock it|1Password app|app:1Password|
1password-cli|Company apps (MDM)|Turn on Integrate with 1Password CLI, then run op whoami in a terminal|1Password → Settings → Developer|app:1Password|op-cli

# ---- Apps not in the Brewfile ----
cursor-nightly|Apps not in the Brewfile|Install Cursor Nightly (separate app, next to the stable Cursor)|cursor.com/nightlydownload|https://cursor.com/nightlydownload|app:/Applications/Cursor Nightly.app
youtube-music|Apps not in the Brewfile|Install YouTube Music as a Chrome app|Chrome → music.youtube.com → ⋮ → Cast, save, and share → Install page as app|https://music.youtube.com|app:@HOME@/Applications/Chrome Apps.localized/YouTube Music.app

# ---- Privacy & Security permissions ----
hammerspoon-ax|Privacy & Security permissions|Allow Hammerspoon (Sidecar → Slack), then restart it and choose Reload Config|System Settings → Privacy & Security → Device Control and Data Access → Hammerspoon|x-apple.systempreferences:com.apple.preference.security?Privacy_Accessibility|hammerspoon-ax
karabiner-driver|Privacy & Security permissions|Enable the Karabiner DriverKit VirtualHIDDevice driver|System Settings → General → Login Items & Extensions → Driver Extensions|x-apple.systempreferences:com.apple.LoginItems-Settings.extension|karabiner-driver
karabiner-ax|Privacy & Security permissions|Allow Karabiner-Elements and Karabiner-Core-Service|System Settings → Privacy & Security → Device Control and Data Access|x-apple.systempreferences:com.apple.preference.security?Privacy_Accessibility|tcc:Accessibility:org.pqrs.Karabiner-Core-Service
karabiner-login-items|Privacy & Security permissions|Allow Karabiner-Elements to run in the background|System Settings → General → Login Items & Extensions → Allow in the Background|x-apple.systempreferences:com.apple.LoginItems-Settings.extension|
raycast-ax|Privacy & Security permissions|Allow Raycast (needed for Clipboard History)|System Settings → Privacy & Security → Device Control and Data Access → Raycast|x-apple.systempreferences:com.apple.preference.security?Privacy_Accessibility|tcc:Accessibility:com.raycast.macos
ghostty-fda|Privacy & Security permissions|Give Ghostty Full Disk Access (lets check.sh read Login Items and Finder Recents)|System Settings → Privacy & Security → Full Disk Access → Ghostty|x-apple.systempreferences:com.apple.preference.security?Privacy_AllFiles|tcc:SystemPolicyAllFiles:com.mitchellh.ghostty
grokbot-fda|Privacy & Security permissions|Give Grok Bot Full Disk Access (for its unattended check.sh runs)|System Settings → Privacy & Security → Full Disk Access → Grok Bot|x-apple.systempreferences:com.apple.preference.security?Privacy_AllFiles|tcc:SystemPolicyAllFiles:com.anysphere.sand

# ---- Trackpad, mouse & pointer ----
trackpad-tap-to-click|Trackpad, mouse & pointer|Trackpad: Tap to click On|System Settings → Trackpad → Point & Click|x-apple.systempreferences:com.apple.Trackpad-Settings.extension|defaults:com.apple.AppleMultitouchTrackpad:Clicking=1
trackpad-click-light|Trackpad, mouse & pointer|Trackpad: Click pressure Light|System Settings → Trackpad → Point & Click → Click|x-apple.systempreferences:com.apple.Trackpad-Settings.extension|defaults:com.apple.AppleMultitouchTrackpad:FirstClickThreshold=0
trackpad-secondary-click|Trackpad, mouse & pointer|Trackpad: Secondary click = Click in bottom right corner|System Settings → Trackpad → Point & Click → Secondary click|x-apple.systempreferences:com.apple.Trackpad-Settings.extension|defaults:com.apple.AppleMultitouchTrackpad:TrackpadCornerSecondaryClick=2,TrackpadRightClick=0
trackpad-lookup-force-click|Trackpad, mouse & pointer|Trackpad: Look up & data detectors Off; Force Click and haptic feedback Off|System Settings → Trackpad → Point & Click|x-apple.systempreferences:com.apple.Trackpad-Settings.extension|
trackpad-tracking-speed|Trackpad, mouse & pointer|Trackpad: Tracking speed Slower|System Settings → Trackpad → Point & Click → Tracking speed|x-apple.systempreferences:com.apple.Trackpad-Settings.extension|
trackpad-three-finger-drag|Trackpad, mouse & pointer|Trackpad: Three-finger drag Off|System Settings → Trackpad → More Gestures|x-apple.systempreferences:com.apple.Trackpad-Settings.extension|defaults:com.apple.AppleMultitouchTrackpad:TrackpadThreeFingerDrag=0
trackpad-dragging|Trackpad, mouse & pointer|Use trackpad for dragging On (Without Drag Lock)|System Settings → Accessibility → Pointer Control → Trackpad Options|x-apple.systempreferences:com.apple.Accessibility-Settings.extension|defaults:com.apple.AppleMultitouchTrackpad:Dragging=1,DragLock=0
pointer-size|Trackpad, mouse & pointer|Pointer size one notch above Normal|System Settings → Accessibility → Display → Pointer → Pointer size|x-apple.systempreferences:com.apple.Accessibility-Settings.extension|pointer-size
mouse-settings|Trackpad, mouse & pointer|Mouse (System Settings): tracking, double-click and scrolling speed faster; secondary click on right side (the wheel's direction, Natural, is set in Logi Options+ and checked by check.sh)|System Settings → Mouse|x-apple.systempreferences:com.apple.Mouse-Settings.extension|
logi-smooth-scrolling|Trackpad, mouse & pointer|Logi Options+: Smooth scrolling On (main wheel and thumb wheel)|Logi Options+ → MX Master 3S → Point & Scroll|app:logioptionsplus|logi:wheel-smooth,thumb-smooth
logi-cloud-backup|Trackpad, mouse & pointer|Logi Options+: sign in and turn on cloud backup (Automatically backup all devices); confirm it shows a recent Last backup|Logi Options+ → MX Master 3S → Settings → Other → Automatically backup all devices|app:logioptionsplus|

# ---- Display, keyboard & desktop ----
display-more-space|Display, keyboard & desktop|Built-in display: More Space|System Settings → Displays|x-apple.systempreferences:com.apple.Displays-Settings.extension|
auto-brightness|Display, keyboard & desktop|Displays: Automatically adjust brightness Off (leave True Tone and Slightly dim the display on battery as they are)|System Settings → Displays|x-apple.systempreferences:com.apple.Displays-Settings.extension|@check.sh
input-british|Display, keyboard & desktop|Keyboard input source: British|System Settings → Keyboard → Text Input → Input Sources|x-apple.systempreferences:com.apple.Keyboard-Settings.extension|input-british
desktop-widgets|Display, keyboard & desktop|Remove all desktop widgets|Desktop: right-click each widget → Remove Widget (System Settings → Desktop & Dock → Widgets)|x-apple.systempreferences:com.apple.Desktop-Settings.extension|
user-picture|Display, keyboard & desktop|Set your user picture to the Dog|System Settings → Users & Groups → your account picture|x-apple.systempreferences:com.apple.Users-Groups-Settings.extension|

# ---- Notifications & Spotlight ----
notifications-mirroring|Notifications & Spotlight|Notifications Off when mirroring or sharing the display|System Settings → Notifications|x-apple.systempreferences:com.apple.Notifications-Settings.extension|
notifications-apps|Notifications & Spotlight|Turn notifications Off for Calendar, Cursor Nightly, FaceTime, Game Center, Home, Mail, Microsoft Teams, Slack, Spotify, Tips, Wallet|System Settings → Notifications → Application Notifications|x-apple.systempreferences:com.apple.Notifications-Settings.extension|
spotlight-results|Notifications & Spotlight|Spotlight: turn Off results from Books, Keynote, Mail, Notes, Numbers, Photos, Podcasts, Reminders, Stocks, Tips, Voice Memos|System Settings → Spotlight → Results from Apps|x-apple.systempreferences:com.apple.Spotlight-Settings.extension|

# ---- Login Items & Finder ----
login-items-off|Login Items & Finder|Keep ChatGPT, Gemini and GeminiAppLauncher Off at login|System Settings → General → Login Items & Extensions|x-apple.systempreferences:com.apple.LoginItems-Settings.extension|@check.sh

# ---- App settings ----
gemini-shortcuts|App settings|Gemini shortcuts: Mini chat Control+Option+G, Full chat Control+Option+Shift+G (defaults clash with ChatGPT)|Gemini → Settings → Shortcuts|app:Gemini|
raycast-import|App settings|Raycast: on a new Mac, import your .rayconfig backup (tick Settings, Aliases & Hotkeys), or set the three Raycast items below by hand; keep Scheduled Backup on (never in this repo: it holds clipboard history and extension settings)|Raycast → Import Settings & Data (backups: Raycast → Settings → Advanced → Export / Scheduled Backup)|app:Raycast|
raycast-hotkey|App settings|Raycast hotkey: Shift+Control+Command+R (off Option+Space, which clashes with ChatGPT)|Raycast → Settings → General → Raycast Hotkey|app:Raycast|defaults:com.raycast.macos:raycastGlobalHotkey=Shift-Control-Command-15
raycast-finder-hotkey|App settings|Raycast: Finder hotkey Shift+Control+Command+F|Raycast → type Finder → Command+K → Configure Application… → Record Hotkey|app:Raycast|
raycast-clipboard|App settings|Raycast Clipboard History: hotkey Control+Command+V, keep history 1 day, disable 1Password and 1Password for Safari|Raycast → Settings → Extensions → Clipboard History|app:Raycast|

# ---- Modes (Hammerspoon menu-bar switcher; see README "Modes") ----
mode-focus-modes|Modes (menu-bar switcher)|Create two Focus modes named WebConf and DeepWork (WebConf: allow Granola; DeepWork: allow Hammerspoon, so the end-of-session notification gets through)|System Settings → Focus → Add Focus… → Custom|x-apple.systempreferences:com.apple.Focus-Settings.extension|@check.sh
mode-focus-shortcuts|Modes (menu-bar switcher)|Create four Shortcuts, each with one Set Focus action: "Mode WebConf On" (Turn WebConf On until Turned Off), "Mode WebConf Off" (Turn WebConf Off), "Mode DeepWork On", "Mode DeepWork Off"|Shortcuts → + → search "Set Focus"|app:Shortcuts|@check.sh
mode-hammerspoon-alerts|Modes (menu-bar switcher)|Hammerspoon notifications: style Alerts, so the DeepWork end-of-session buttons (Take a break / Back to Normal / Another session) show|System Settings → Notifications → Hammerspoon → Alerts|x-apple.systempreferences:com.apple.Notifications-Settings.extension|
mode-menubar-pin|Modes (menu-bar switcher)|Pin the mode-switcher menu-bar icon so it stays visible: hold Command (⌘) and drag it toward Control Centre / the clock, because icons further from them get auto-hidden behind <<|Menu bar → ⌘-drag the mode icon (desktop computer / red ⏺ / brain)||
